; renamesetup.eval — the scratch world the rename checks run in (W11), run with
; -project wt_ren after WorldTest has made it. It authors EVERY kind of
; reference to a dungeon and a level that lives outside the level being
; renamed, so the rename has something to miss:
;   - a doorway named the SHORT way (id = the dungeon's, no dungeon= field)
;   - a doorway with an explicit level=, and the starter's own (keep_gate)
;   - the game's opening, and the harness level (the starter's eval_level)
;   - a stair on ANOTHER level leading into the one renamed
;   - a location whose id is spelled like the level (room1), which an EXIT
;     stair names — WorldTest writes that stair in by hand, since no command
;     can author an exit
; The opening is set BEFORE `levels new`, whose project save is what writes it.
logecho on
reset
worldloc add dungeon keep 3 3
worldloc set keep level room1
worldprops opening keep room1 8 8
levels new keep
stairadd stairs_down 7 7
worldloc add dungeon room1 4 4
worldloc set room1 dungeon keep
worldloc set room1 level keep1
savemap
